# armour/shared/pauldron_layered3_r: the medium LAYERED pauldron on the right shoulder (layered.3; FORGE-SHOULDERS, STYLE_P2 28.3).
# lamellar flaps laced in steps: each row of lamellae a step lower and a pixel further out, its lacing a row of
# dots (Jade, Steppe, Dune, Marsh, Sylvan).
# Rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`). Finish regions: R the lowest flap's hem, G the top lacing knot, N the lacing rows, P the flaps.
# Shared by the man and the woman (D10). Generated by FORGE-SHOULDERS gen.py from shapes.py (re-run, never hand-edit
# the derived views). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
role pauldron layered.3
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R

view D key rest origin 4 3
|....vvvv
|..vvxxwv
|.vxxxxwv
|vwwwwwwv
|.vyyyyxv
|vwwwwwwv
|.vyyyyv.
|.vxxxxv.
|vwwwwwv.
|.vxxxxv.
|vwwwwwv.
|.vvvvv..
regions
|........
|....PPP.
|........
|.NNNNNN.
|........
|.NNNNNN.
|........
|........
|.NNNNN..
|........
|.NNNNN..
|........
# (P5b2, C3d) a polearm carried at T3: the fist grips the haft at the hem of the sode (the jade3 glaive, D rest: the grip at
# rows 10-11), so the sode ends two lames shorter, above the fist (the same lames, its hem row closed; before the T3 view: the first `replace` that holds wins)
view D key rest origin 3 3 when armour.t3,!armour.t4,spear replace
|....vvv
|..vxxwv
|.vxxxwv
|vwwwwwv
|.vyyyxv
|vwwwwwv
|.vyyyv.
|.vxxxv.
|vwwwwv.
|.vvvvv.
regions
|.......
|...PPP.
|.......
|.NNNNN.
|.......
|.NNNNN.
|.......
|.......
|.NNNN..
|.......

